From 6a8c0d346aed9179c9a2b58b82ccd00f0d28d9c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:20:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Retry kept server fallbacks like other suspended
 boundaries

Follow-ups for keeping the server fallback of a browser-only boundary while
its client render is suspended:

- Retry at a normal retry lane once the content is unblocked. The kept
  boundary used the dehydrated state's OffscreenLane, so the content was
  retried at idle priority and could wait behind an unrelated suspended
  transition.
- Honor ScheduleRetry when completing a kept boundary, like any boundary
  showing its fallback. Otherwise skipped siblings were not prerendered and
  content that suspends the commit on a stylesheet was never retried.
- Don't keep the server fallback if a context it could read has changed, and
  retry a kept boundary when a parent context changes, like a client
  rendered boundary showing its fallback. Otherwise the fallback could go
  stale, and content unblocked by the context change stayed hidden.
- Gate on didReceiveUpdate so legacy context changes are covered too.
- The deletion of the dehydrated fragment is already dropped when the client
  render attempt unwinds, so just clear the leftover ChildDeletion flag.
- Suppress the invalid-compare Flow error for renderers without hydration,
  like the same comparison in the first pass.
